cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scCAT in your research, please cite the following paper."
title: "scCAT: confidence-weighted adaptive triplet learning for single-cell data integration"
abstract: >
  scCAT is a single-cell RNA-seq batch-integration method that combines
  confidence-weighted triplet construction, adaptive margins and
  batch-specific local-topology protection.  It is designed for
  compositionally unbalanced datasets where some cell populations are
  batch-specific, and it explicitly avoids overcorrection of cells that
  lack reliable cross-batch counterparts.
